What is GitOps?
 GitOps is a modern DevOps practice where Git is used as the single source of truth for declarative infrastructure and applications. It allows automated deployment, monitoring, and management of your infrastructure using Git repositories.

History of GitOps:
Coined by Weaveworks in 2017
Designed to simplify Kubernetes operations
Built on the principles of Git + CI/CD + Kubernetes automation

Why GitOps is trending in DevOps:
Automates deployments and reduces manual errors ⚡
Provides version control and rollback capabilities using Git
Ensures continuous reconciliation of infrastructure and apps
Enhances collaboration across teams

💡 Fun Fact: GitOps isn’t just for Kubernetes! Any system that supports declarative configuration can leverage GitOps principles.
